  "notes": "Christmas Island District High School, run by Western Australia's Department of Education, teaches Pre-primary to Year 12 on its main site, with Kindergarten at a separate centre, and follows WA's structure. In WA, Kindergarten (age 4 by 30 June) is not compulsory and is left out; Pre-primary (5 by 30 June) is the first compulsory year and Australia's Foundation year. Year 7 starts secondary. Years 11–12 lead to the WACE by university-entrance or vocational pathways, with some classes through SIDE distance education."
